 "content": "# Continual-ARC task 8186789e — verified rule\n\nA grid is partitioned into equal-sized panels by full-width/full-height separator lines. Copy the contents of the one patterned panel into every other panel, preserving each cell's relative position within its panel; keep separators unchanged. In the observed demo, background was 8, vertical separator color 4, and an 8x8 source pattern in panel 1 was repeated into panels 2 and 3. In the solved test, background was 6, divider color 1, vertical dividers at columns 4 and 8 (1-indexed), and horizontal divider at row 5; the 3x4 upper-left panel pattern was repeated across all 3 columns and both rows of panels, while all dividers stayed intact. The correct test output was the 3x3 tiling of the upper-left 4x3 motif into all six panels. This rule was verified by a correct submission. Be careful that input motif cells (including non-background colors) are copied exactly, not transformed."
